What:		/sys/devices/system/node/has_user_memory
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux Memory Management list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Nodelist of the memory nodes that userspace may place memory on,
		i.e. those that may appear in an mbind(2), set_mempolicy(2),
		move_pages(2) or migrate_pages(2) node set.

		Every ordinary node is listed.  A memory node absent from this
		list is hosted by a device that did not opt into userspace
		placement: naming it on its own is rejected with EINVAL, and
		naming it alongside other nodes simply drops it from the set.

What:		/sys/devices/system/node/has_fallback_memory
Date:		July 2026
Contact:	Linux Memory Management list <linux-mm@kvack.org>
Description:
		Nodelist of the memory nodes on the page allocator's fallback
		zonelists, i.e. those an allocation can reach without asking for
		them by name.

		Every ordinary node is listed.  A memory node absent from this
		list is hosted by a device and only ever receives memory that
		was explicitly bound to it, so its capacity must not be counted
		towards what an unbound allocation can obtain.  Such a node may
		still appear in has_user_memory, meaning it can be bound to
		deliberately.
